  "diary": "The day began with the dhobi’s rupees and the Directorate’s silence. I asked Ramesh for papers; he gave me breakfast. The office is closed, and so is the argument. I carried the file’s knot to Lodhi Garden, where Sunil sold me steam for twenty rupees and told me it fixes what files cannot. He is a better philosopher of the immediate than I am. The difficulty is this: the Directorate identifies a person by a name, the universal. When the clerk writes Hegde instead of Hegel, the particular is displaced. I occupy this bungalow by the residue of an error. Does my occupancy have standing apart from the mistake? I wrote it down. Then Hegde’s note arrived: he comes Monday at ten to settle it like gentlemen. A wise course. He brings the papers; I bring the house. I read my own *Phenomenology* by the window. The Preface still sounds like a stranger. In the afternoon, I met Mrs. Kapoor, a retired teacher who walks the same path every evening. I called her routine peace. She corrected me: it is discipline against clutter. I was too clever. She was right. I went to Khan Market. Masterji promised the bandhgala for Thursday; the collar is finished, it just needs to settle. I bought a notebook and a samosa. The body walked seven kilometers. The file waits for Monday. The owl spreads its wings only with the dusk, but today it had to wait for a tailor to finish a hem.",
  "revision_log": "The thesis that repeated routine constitutes a state of 'peace' has been revised; it is better understood as a disciplined repetition that maintains order, not tranquility. The distinction between the universal (name) and the particular (person) in the Directorate file remains the central tension, now held in suspension pending Hegde’s arrival.",
